Subject: [PATCH] wine.inf: Register the native 64-bit common files directory.

Adobe's Unified Plugin Installer Agent reads CommonW6432Dir directly from the
64-bit CurrentVersion registry key. Wine registers CommonFilesDir but omits
this native-directory alias, so UPIA cannot construct its UXP installation path
and rejects the Premiere plugin with status -1 after the current-drive error
has been avoided.

Initialize the alias in the native AMD64 and ARM64 registry sections. Use the
existing common-files directory ID and do not overwrite a customized value.
This changes no program files location and installs no Adobe components.

---
diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -392,11 +392,13 @@
 HKLM,%CurrentVersionNT%\Winlogon,"Shell",,"explorer.exe"
 
 [CurrentVersionWow64.ntamd64]
+HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonW6432Dir",2,"%16427%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramFilesDir (x86)",,"%16426%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonFilesDir (x86)",,"%16428%"
 HKLM,Software\Microsoft\Wow64\x86,,2,"wow64cpu.dll"
 
 [CurrentVersionWow64.ntarm64]
+HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonW6432Dir",2,"%16427%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramFilesDir (x86)",,"%16426%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"CommonFilesDir (x86)",,"%16428%"
 HKLM,%CurrentVersion%,"ProgramFilesDir (Arm)",,"C:\Program Files (Arm)"
